 "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n5le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "Paradigms in programming are going to remain essential for a very long time. There are two existing approaches to writing a program: procedure-oriented programming (POP) and object-oriented programming (OOP). You ought to write a program using the paradigm that best fits your experience and knowledge, yet there are differences between both approaches. As a professional, you will always want to know what those differences are. It doesn't matter if you might want to focus on object-oriented programming as it is the most popular paradigm nowadays.", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "34500", "text": "From the moment computers were invented, many different ways of programming have been tried out: top-down programming, bottom-up programming, modular programming, structured programming, etc. They all have specific and basic purposes to make programming efficient. What will you be expecting from such approaches? Well, they should make the language for writing a program easier, bug-free, less hard to understand, easily modifiable, etc.", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "63000", "text": "As a programmer, I can say you had better learn some aspects that help you to differentiate POP from OOP and its basic units. There's a set of instructions to be followed step by step. You are going to be facing various levels of difficulty regarding program writing for our class. Here are some facts: For developing a fairly complex program, you will choose a procedural approach (POP). If you are good at programming with POP, you might want to do the same with a more complex program, but actually, you are going to be working with OOP. OOP allows collaborative working, which is what we are looking for in our projects for next year. The main reason for this is code reusability; you work on a particular piece of code for next week, but one of your programmers can reuse it as many times as he wants for the oncoming projects. This makes software development much faster and efficient.", "image": "enpe7n5le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le01ob02re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}